Jimlock3000 schrieb:
> 
> Sometime early in my current game I displeased Set, and now all of my
> sacrifices yield, "You have a feeling of inadequacy."  I just killed a
> dragon, which apparently I should sacrifice to get back in His chaotic
> graces.  But how can I get the dragon corpse to the chaotic altar one
> level above?

You can't. Dragon corpses are too heavy to lift, even for
maximum-strength characters with no inventory.

AFAIK, living dragons will not use staircases unless they're your pet,
which also excludes turning the dragon alive again and luring it to
the altar.

> I have teleport control, and a wand of teleportation, so I guess I
> could get zap to the stairs (?)

Teleport control allows you to give a destination when your character
gets teleported. You can't control where items get teleported. And you
still wouldn't get it up the stairs ...

You'll have to go back to the altar and find something on that level;
and if it's big (baluchitherium, dragon, grown naga, centaur, giant),
you'll have to kill it on top of the altar, or you can't sacrifice it.

